CLAIM 15 — Local Claude Code / Codex CLI workers

Scope of inspection (static only): src/goal/cli-worker.ts,
src/goal/cli-runner.ts, src/goal/backend-types.ts,
src/goal/backend-availability.ts, src/goal/claude-code-env.ts,
src/config/types.goal.ts.

What the code actually does
============================

A. The supported backends are the local Codex CLI and the local Claude Code
   CLI; no in-process model API call is used to drive a worker step.

   - src/goal/backend-types.ts:7-10 — `export const SUPPORTED_BACKEND_IDS =
     ["codex", "claude_code"] as const;` (only these two values are accepted
     anywhere downstream; full file establishes the GoalBackendId union and
     transport contract).
   - src/goal/backend-availability.ts:114-148 — `probeBackend` shells out to
     `codex --version` / `claude --version` (or equivalent) and records
     whether each CLI is installed on PATH before a worker is dispatched.

B. The worker invocation is a real subprocess against the local CLI binary.

   - src/goal/cli-worker.ts:183 — `const command = backend === "codex"
     ? "codex" : "claude";` (used by the repair pass).
   - src/goal/cli-worker.ts:288 — same selection in the main attempt path:
     `const command = backend === "codex" ? "codex" : "claude";`
   - src/goal/cli-worker.ts:327-336 — `runCliProcess({ command, args, cwd:
     workingDir, ..., env: workerEnv })` runs the chosen CLI; stdout and
     stderr stream to per-attempt files inside the run's worker directory.
   - src/goal/cli-worker.ts:782-799 — Codex arg builder spawns
     `codex [--ask-for-approval never] exec --json --sandbox workspace-write
     --cd <workingDir> -c net.allowed=true [--model <id>] <prompt>`.
   - src/goal/cli-worker.ts:802-816 — Claude Code arg builder spawns
     `claude -p --verbose --output-format stream-json --allowedTools <list>
     --append-system-prompt <denies+context> [--model <id>] <prompt>`.

C. Claude Code is wired for *subscription* auth by default — credential env
   vars are scrubbed so the Claude Code CLI uses its own configured auth.

   - src/config/types.goal.ts:1 — `export type ClaudeCodeAuthMode =
     "subscription" | "api_key";`
   - src/goal/cli-worker.ts:230 — `claudeCodeAuth = "subscription"` is the
     default when `executeTaskWithCliWorker` is called without an explicit
     mode.
   - src/goal/cli-worker.ts:249-250 — `const workerEnv = buildGoalWorkerEnv(
     backend, claudeCodeAuth);` and `if (backend === "claude_code")
     writeAuthModeArtifact(workerDir, claudeCodeAuth);` — the resolved auth
     mode is persisted to `auth_mode.txt` in the worker dir for audit.
   - src/goal/claude-code-env.ts:7-11 — `AUTH_KEYS_TO_STRIP = [
     "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY", "ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN", "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_OLD" ]`.
   - src/goal/claude-code-env.ts:54-67 — `buildClaudeCodeEnv("subscription")`
     deletes those keys from the env before spawning `claude`, so the CLI
     falls back to its own subscription-based login. (`"api_key"` mode
     passes the gateway's ANTHROPIC_API_KEY through.)

D. The harness does not embed an Anthropic/OpenAI SDK call to do the worker
   step itself — every worker call goes through the locally installed CLI
   binary. The Node code only handles prompt assembly, subprocess
   management, log capture, and result-JSON parsing.

