Safe README wording
===================
- "Each worker step is executed by a locally installed CLI — Codex
  (`codex exec ...`) or Claude Code (`claude -p ...`). Moltbot uses local
  CLI backends; it does not call a model API directly to drive worker
  steps."
- "Claude Code workers run in subscription auth mode by default: the
  harness strips `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`-class environment variables from the
  worker process so the Claude Code CLI uses whatever credentials it has
  been configured with."
- "Whether each CLI is available is probed at run dispatch; if a backend
  is not installed on PATH, the run falls back to whichever backend is."

Unsafe wording to avoid
=======================
- "Free Claude / unlimited Codex." (No claim of free or unlimited use —
  the harness only delegates to whatever subscription/billing the
  installed CLI itself has.)
- "Bring-your-own API key required." (Subscription mode does not require
  an API key for the worker.)
- "Moltbot ships its own model runtime." (It does not — it shells out to
  the local CLIs.)
- "Works without the Codex or Claude Code CLI installed." (The probe
  fails closed: an uninstalled CLI is reported unavailable.)

STATUS: verified
REASON: Both worker backends are real subprocess invocations of the
locally installed `codex` and `claude` binaries (cli-worker.ts:183, 288,
327-336, 782-816). Claude Code defaults to subscription auth and the
harness strips Anthropic credential env vars so the CLI uses its own
login (claude-code-env.ts:54-67). Safe README wording is "uses local CLI
backends"; do not promise free or unlimited usage.
